Assume now that $l \geq 3$. Since every point in the set $\bar{S}$, excluding those   corresponding to the maximum and minimum of the variables $\lambda$ and $\nu$, represents a double point of $\bar{\gamma}$, Claim5 tells us that the remaining $\# S_0 - k =  k (l-1)$ points in $S_0$ represent self-intersections of the  $\gamma$, see Figure \ref{fig:ex2}.
