\noindent
\textbf{Fact(2o).} There exist values $0 < \lambda_1 < \cdots < \lambda_{(l-1)/2} < \lambda_{\max}$ and $-\pi < \nu_1 < \cdots < \nu_k < 0$, such  that
the self-intersection points of the collision-collision orbit $K$ lie at the intersections of the ellipses $\lambda = \lambda_j$ and the hyperbolae $\nu = \nu_i$, see Figure \ref{fig:examplesforRemark}.

