By linear SDEs' estimates, we can obtain (\ref{est diff1}).
Moreover,
\begin{equation*}
	\check{u}_{1i}^+(\cdot)-u_{1i}^+(\cdot)=-\left(\tilde{R}_1+L^{\top}\tilde{R}_0L\right)^{-1}\left(\tilde{B}+\tilde{H}L\right)^\top\Sigma\left(\check{x}_i(\cdot)-x_i^+(\cdot)\right).
\end{equation*}
Consequently, by (\ref{est diff1}), we have (\ref{est diff2}).
