		\begin{abstract}
We show that the Grauert blow-down of a holomorphic negative line bundle $L$ over a compact complex space is a quadratic transform if and only if $k_0L^*$ is very ample and $(k_0+1)L^*$ is globally generated,
where $k_0$ is the initial order of $L^*$, namely, the minimal integer such that $k_0L^*$ has nontrivial holomorphic section.
		\end{abstract}

