    It follows that for $\hat\theta \in X_3$, the function $\theta_1 \mapsto \ubar v_1\left(tr \mid \theta_1, \sigma_2^{\hat\theta} \right)$ is strictly decreasing on $X_2 \cup X_3$.
    Moreover, 
    \begin{align*}
        \ubar v_1\left(tr \mid F_h^{-1}\left(\tfrac{1}{2}\right), \sigma_2^{\hat\theta} \right)=\tfrac{1}{2}\geq F_l\left(F_h^{-1}\left(\tfrac{1}{2}\right)\right) = \ubar v_1\left(nt \mid F_h^{-1}\left(\tfrac{1}{2}\right), \sigma_2^{\hat\theta} \right)
