The challenge is thus how to build and train a general world model. 
Based on our analysis and common practices in machine learning, the keys to building such a world model include:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Identifying \textbf{data} with the desired world information
    \item Finding a general \textbf{representation} space for the latent world state, with possibly richer information than the observation data
    \item Adopting an \textbf{architecture} that effectively reasons over the representations
    \item Developing an \textbf{objective} that efficiently trains the world model
    \item Determine how to \textbf{use} the world model in decision-making systems
\end{enumerate}
A survey reveals that current implementations of world model fall short in a variety of ways including domain generality, world completeness, controllability, practical usability, among others.  
