\subsection{Usage: MPC or RL?}
\label{subsec:usage}

\begin{displayquote}
\textit{Abandon reinforcement learning (RL); adopt model-predictive control (MPC) for fewer trials required during training.}
\end{displayquote}


% Beyond training world models, this school of thought further advocates discarding reinforcement learning (RL) in favor of model-predictive control (MPC) due to efficiency advantages (cite Chelsea Finn). This typical MPC setup involves initializing an action sequence, simulating the future latent states using the world model, and optimizing actions with respect to a given objective (e.g., progress towards a goal). The appeal of MPC lies in learning from offline trajectories without potentially unsafe exploration in the real world, as well as potential for higher-quality decision-making from world-model-based simulation. 
% \eric{More details are needed here: how many latent spaces to simulate? over how many combinations of actions in a sequence? Exactly how optimization takes place over it? ...If possible sketch the algorithm.} 
