\begin{document}

\begin{abstract}
We establish a connection between multiple polylogarithms on a torus and 
the Steinberg module of $\Q$, and show that multiple polylogarithms of depth $d$ and weight $n$ can be expressed via a single function $\Li_{n-d+1,1,\dots,1}(x_1,x_2,\dots,x_d)$. Using this connection, we give a simple proof of the Bykovski\u{\i} theorem, explain the duality between multiple polylogarithms and iterated integrals, and provide a polylogarithmic interpretation of the conjectures of Rognes and Church-Farb-Putman. 
\end{abstract}

